id: pm-8we38i
title: Refresh review acknowledgements when bot feedback changes
description: "Make complete review inventories identify content revisions and make acknowledgement retries idempotent for the reviewed revision, so edited comments cannot retain a stale handled result. Preserve check-driven waits and real inline reply surfaces."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-06T05:17:54.521Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-06T14:44:20.497Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-06T14:14:52.971Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-06T14:14:52.971Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: An edited bot body has a new revision identity; unchanged acknowledgement retries create no duplicate; changed feedback gets a fresh explanation; inline and top-level surfaces remain distinct; exact-head inventory and required check watches remain complete
value: Prevent stale review decisions and reduce repeated feedback cost
outcome: Every current bot revision has an explicit attributable disposition
why_now: The requested review loop requires checking edited feedback before merge; current acknowledgement markers identify only the artifact
parent: pm-0fxa
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Preserved revision-scoped and thread-scoped acknowledgements while projecting unused REST payload fields and defining a 64 MiB complete-response transport bound with visible overflow failure.
expected_result: Large review conversations remain completely inventoried and acknowledgeable without duplicate replies or silent truncation.
actual_result: "Real 2 MiB child-process red/green regression, all 14 helper tests, linked verification, focused ESLint and docs links pass. Live projected GitHub lookup retained 84 comments in 89639 bytes and the previously failing acknowledgements completed."
